---
layout: _base.njk
header: minimal
title: Hire me for agency or in-house work | Francesco Imola
description: Open to agency overflow, freelance briefs and in-house roles. UX, copywriting, brand messaging and email marketing, from a designer based in Kent.
contentMode: contrast
eleventyNavigation:
  key: Collaborate
  parent: Home
---
{% from "_project-item.njk" import projectItem %}
{% from "_cta-card.njk" import ctaCard %}
{% from "_quote-card.njk" import quoteCard %}
<header class="collab-hero">
    <div class="flow has-gap-s">
        <h1 class="headline">Web and content designer based in Folkestone, Kent.</h1>
        <p>I help people with big ideas get their big ideas across.</p>
        <p>I’ve been called a “dream collaborator”, the one who goes “above and beyond”, “so deeply reliable” and many other things, but I tend to describe myself as an intermediary between people’s ambitious ideas and their tangible results.</p>
        <p>Say you're launching a new film: I deal less with questions like “How do we become the most talked about film of the year”, and more with questions like “How do we reach the communities that would connect most with this film? How do we get them to watch it, and from there reach even wider audiences?”.</p>
        <p>In the day to day, my fortes are information architecture, trust-based marketing, and design: UX, UI, graphic, and content.</p>
        <p>I’ve worked with freelancers, solo owners, boutique agencies, small businesses, and institutional departments, across education, nonprofit, B2B, and B2C.</p>
        <p>Feel like I could be the person you’re after?</p>
        {# status is a span, not a p — the button sits inline and a p can't nest inside a p #}
        <p><button type="button" data-copy-email="hi@francescoimola.com" data-icon="copy">Copy email address</button><span role="status" class="sr-only" data-copy-status></span></p>
        <a href="/about/" data-icon="arrow-right">More about me</a>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-cols-2 collab-hero__photos">
        <div class="duotone">
            <img src="/assets/images/francesco-bw.png" alt="Francesco Imola" style="aspect-ratio: var(--ratio-3-4)">
        </div>
        <div class="duotone">
            <img src="/assets/images/francesco-presentation.png" alt="Francesco Imola presenting" style="aspect-ratio: var(--ratio-1-1)">
        </div>
    </div>
</header>
<section class="section">
    <h2 class="highlight-header">What I do</h2>
    <ul class="flow has-gap-xs">
        {% for service in collaborate.services %}
        <li class="card"><strong>{{ service.title }}</strong><span class="dimmed"><br>{{ service.description }}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</section>
<section class="home-block flow has-gap-s-m" aria-labelledby="featured-work">
    <h2 id="featured-work">Featured work</h2>
    {% for slug in collaborate.featured %}
    {% for project in collections.work %}{% if project.fileSlug == slug %}
    {{ projectItem(project.data.title, project.data.services, project.data.image, project.data.alt, project.url or "") }}
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
</section>
<section class="section">
    <h2 class="highlight-header">Can we rely on him?</h2>
    <div class="flow has-gap-s">
        <p>I’ll stick around no matter how messy things get, as long as I'm working with people who care deeply about what they do as much as they care about each other.</p>
        <p>Found yourself in uncharted waters? We'll cross them together. Is your design or marketing team struggling to agree on what needs doing? I may not have all the answers, but I'll support them as they search for them.</p>
        {% for t in testimonials.collaborate %}{{ quoteCard(t) }}{% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>
<section class="section">
    <h2 class="highlight-header">What does he have that others don't?</h2>
    <div class="flow has-gap-s">
        <p>Many of the talented people you could hire will be able to come up with spectacular visual concepts, which is fantastic for them and for their clients.</p>
        <p>But what would they say if you asked them to reveal their thought process, or explain how they intend to guide a user from point A to point B?</p>
        <p>If all you need is pretty graphics, I'm afraid you have to look elsewhere. By contrast, if you're looking for a partner in crime who can guide you, help you make important decisions, write your content AND give you thoughtful results on the visual front, then I'm your guy.</p>
        <p>Drawing on my skills in graphic design, UX, UI and content writing—and on 8 years of experience in inbound marketing—I take an annoyingly thorough approach to my work, I'm not scared of revisions, and I bend over backwards (for which we have to thank my yoga teacher!) to deliver pretty good results 99% of the time.</p>
    </div>
</section>
{{ ctaCard(
    "I don't bite",
    "Say hello. Let's chat about what you need and maybe we'll grab a coffee if you're nearby.",
    emailFirst = true
) }}
